# Data and large files, never committed.
# The leading slash is required: without it the rule matches a data/ directory at
# any depth, including src/data/, and silently ignores source files that belong
# in the repository. A script was lost that way once.
/data/
*.stl
*.nrrd
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.ply
*.obj
*.npz
# ...except the defect-region labels, which are tracked (66 KB). They are an
# INPUT to evaluation rather than a product: the defect region is defined by the
# dataset's implant ground truth, and this is where those labels live. Producing
# them needs the raw volumes and marching cubes, and the raw data is not tracked
# -- so without this line, losing the raw data means losing the ability to
# recompute any historical metric.
!experiments_log/defect_mask_labels.npz
*.npy
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.h5
experiments/
# Rendered figures are ignored by default, so that re-running the figure script
# does not sweep a pile of new images into the index. The delivered ones are
# force-added instead.
#
# The rule originally assumed every figure could be regenerated from the archived
# runs. That stopped being true once checkpoints were pruned: some figures depend
# on runs whose weights are gone, and training is not bit-reproducible, so they
# cannot be redrawn. Storing a few megabytes of finished figures is cheaper than
# keeping gigabytes of superseded weights to preserve the option.
reports/figures/*.png
reports/*.pptx
# mesh_preview.py's HTML output: 20-40 MB each, something to look at rather than
# a deliverable.
reports/preview/

# Specific to one deployment rather than to the project: personal environment
# setup, the backup script for this machine's network disk, the command sheet
# that goes with them, and the editor tasks that drive them.
setup_local.sh
sync_workspace.sh
RUNBOOK.md
.vscode/tasks.json
